{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Strong negative bias (systematic under-forecast): true outcomes are consistently above model paths, often by ~+2 to +10 EUR, with the gap widening during sustained rallies. Apply an upward level shift, increasing with recent momentum/volatility.",
    "Trend/acceleration lag: model reacts too slowly to regime shifts upward (fails to capture multi-week uptrend). Add a momentum term: if last 5–10 days slope is positive, steepen the forecast trajectory (higher drift) rather than reverting to ~70–75.",
    "Horizon-dependent error: underprediction grows with horizon (largest errors mid-to-late forecast window in Examples 1–4). Use a ramping correction (small adjustment days 1–5, larger adjustment days 10–30) when trend is strong.",
    "Over-imposed mean reversion: forecasts repeatedly pull back toward a mid-70s anchor even when realized prices stay elevated (80+). Reduce mean-reversion strength when price breaks above recent range/highs (e.g., above 20–30d high).",
    "Post-peak downside bias/overshoot: when the model finally turns down (Example 5), it drops too far/fast versus outcomes (predicts high-60s while realized stays ~78–80). Damp negative moves after an uptrend; cap daily declines and keep forecasts closer to an elevated plateau unless confirmed by recent declines."
  ]
}
